commit 42d449d152d5c8925c47983c3ea814be85e55a93

C03: the package-status final reads split lists (installed in, not installed in, no pip in) and cannot deny an installation the receipt shows (PIP1819)

PIP1817 measured: given the per-Python list (installed true/false per entry) the small model generalized from its first entry («numpy no está instalado en ninguna versión», «Pandas is not installed. It is available in…»). The composer now projects the receipt as installedIn (with the package version), notInstalledIn and noPipIn, the lens reads those lists, and a final that denies an installation listed in installedIn, or asserts one when the list is empty, is a package_state_reversed defect with its own hint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


